HM: the build's outputs where the build is told to put them

BBuildEnv writes every library and program into the source tree, under lib/ and bin/, whatever directory CMake was given to build in. Two builds of one source tree -- two instruction sets, or Windows and Linux from one checkout -- then write TAppDecoder to the same file, and each takes whichever was built last: MediaPerch's Windows build ran a Linux TAppDecoder, which Windows refused to start. BBuildEnv_OUTPUT_ROOT now says where lib/ and bin/ go, and is the source tree when nobody says, as before. Against HM-16.26.

diff --git a/cmake/CMakeBuild/cmake/modules/BBuildEnv.cmake b/cmake/CMakeBuild/cmake/modules/BBuildEnv.cmake
index 07532ba3..13c0886c 100644
